<title>UK: PPL gets go-ahead for cystic fibrosis tests.</title>
<headline>PPL gets go-ahead for cystic fibrosis tests.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British biotechnology company PPL Therapeutics Plc said on Wednesday it had won approval from UK regulatory authorities to start Phase II testing of its transgenic antitrypsin (TgAAT) treatment for cystic fibrosis.</p>
<p>PPL said cystic fibrosis was the most common fatal genetic disease among caucasians. PPL said it completed Phase I trials last month which indicated the safety of the drug.  </p>
<p>PPL hit the headlines earlier this year by announcing it had cloned an adult sheep.</p>
<p>PPL's shares closed trade at 395p on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
